-- title:
--   Tame generator at a deep level with prescribed divisibilities
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $G_q$ denote `primeLocalGaloisGroup q`, the group of $\mathbb{Q}_q$-automorphisms of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}_q$; let $r =$ `primeLocalToGlobal q` be the homomorphism $G_q \to \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ obtained by restricting scalars to $\mathbb{Q}$ and then restricting to the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $A =$ `primeLocalPlace q` be the valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ pulled back from the $q$-adic integers along the chosen embedding. Let $\varphi \in G_q$ be such that $r(\varphi)$ lies in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acts on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^q$; let $F_0$ be a finite intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, and let $n, d$ be positive integers with $q \nmid n$. Write $I$ for the preimage under $r$ of the image in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and, for an intermediate field $F$, $U_F$ for the preimage under $r$ of the subgroup of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ fixing $F$ pointwise. The assertion is that there exist a finite Galois intermediate field $F \supseteq F_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, an element $t \in I$ and a normal subgroup $W \trianglelefteq G_q$ such that $U_F \le W \le I \vee U_F$; every $w \in W$ satisfies $w^{q^a} \in U_F$ for some $a \in \mathbb{N}$; every $i \in I$ satisfies $(t^a)^{-1} i \in W$ for some $a \in \mathbb{N}$; $(t^q)^{-1}\varphi t \varphi^{-1} \in W$; the image $\bar t$ of $t$ in $G_q/W$ has finite order, divisible by $n$; the subgroup $\langle \bar t\rangle$ generated by $\bar t$ is normal in $G_q/W$; the order $f$ of the image of $\bar\varphi$ in $(G_q/W)/\langle \bar t\rangle$ is divisible by $d$; and $\bar\varphi^{\,f} = \bar t^{\,j}$ for some $j \in \mathbb{N}$ with $n \mid j$.
--
--   This records the tame presentation data of the local Galois group at $q$ at a sufficiently deep finite level: modulo the subgroup $W$ (whose elements become trivial on $F$ after raising to a $q$-power, so that $W$ plays the role of wild inertia together with $U_F$) the quotient is generated by a tame inertia generator $\bar t$ and a Frobenius $\bar\varphi$ subject to $\bar\varphi \bar t \bar\varphi^{-1} = \bar t^{\,q}$, and the level $F$ is chosen so that the order of $\bar t$ is divisible by $n$, the residue degree $f$ by $d$, and $\bar\varphi^{\,f}$ is a $n$-th power of $\bar t$. It strengthens [`ExtCitation.exists_tame_generator_at_level`](thm.html#ExtCitation.exists_tame_generator_at_level) by the divisibility conditions, and is used in the bound [`groupCohomology.invariants_add_dualTwist_le_finrank_continuousClasses`](thm.html#groupCohomology.invariants_add_dualTwist_le_finrank_continuousClasses) for the local term at $q$.
